WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.135
BEAR GRYLLS: OK, Rob.

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.336
Your front points--
your crampons

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.171
are your main
weight-bearing things.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.639
Good lord.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.375
BEAR GRYLLS (VOICEOVER):
Comedian Rob Riggle and I are

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:11.344
in a race against time,
searching to find a case

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.446
of supplies before nightfall.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:18.451
But first, we've got to
scale this mountain of ice.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.120
BEAR GRYLLS: So you're
watching the black ropes.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.387
We're not kicking into that.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.929
Oh, it's a long way down.

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:34.167
Looking at this, it's only
like a 30 or 40-foot ice climb.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.436
But it's what's behind Rob.

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:40.039
There's a 150-foot deep crevasse
that I can see below him.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.208
[panting]

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.643
BEAR GRYLLS: Take your time.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.611
That's good.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:50.683
No hurry.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.919
[blowing]

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.453
ROB RIGGLE: OK, come on, Rob.

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:57.424
What was the one lesson you
learned from basic training?

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.559
Slow and steady wins the race?

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:00.193
Never quit?

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.995
There you go.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:03.596
That is you.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.164
You never quit.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.100
Looking really good.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.835
Finish strong the last bit.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.704
[panting]

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:20.479
Well done.

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:21.314
Well done.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.282
OK, keep using your points now.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:23.883
You can stand up a bit more.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:24.751
Well done.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.986
All right.

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.054
That gets your sweat going, huh?

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:31.056
[laughs] Good job.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.091
It was a good climb.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.626
That's a great motor.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:34.828
It's a great motor--

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:39.966
it's a great motivator
having a 150-foot crevasse

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.434
right behind you.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.636
That kind of gets
you up the hill.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.972
Crossing these things
is always such hard work.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:50.076
It's like, you know, 200 meters
in a straight line, two hours,

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:50.910
you know?

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:51.945
Exactly.

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:52.845
Well done, mate.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:53.947
Thanks.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:54.814
He's panting.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:55.648
He's sweating.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:56.316
He's done well.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.383
We're at the top.

